a:["$","section",null,{"className":"section reveal is-in","id":"overview","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"sec-head","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"kicker","children":"Overview"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"Creating tokens on BNB Smart Chain."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-sec","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"All tokens on BNB Smart Chain are smart contracts deployed to the network. When you “create a token”, you are really deploying a contract that follows the BEP-20 standard — this is what gives the token its balances, transfers and approvals."}],["$","p",null,{"children":["You may see the network referred to as ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"BSC"}]," (BNB Smart Chain) or ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"BNB Chain"}]," — they describe the same network, launched in 2020 as Binance Smart Chain and later ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://www.bnbchain.org/en/blog/bsc-is-now-bnb-chain-the-infrastructure-for-the-metafi-universe","children":"rebranded by the official BNB Chain announcement"}],". On all these names, the token standard is BEP-20 and the chain ID is 56, so a token created through this flow is compatible with the wallets, exchanges and explorers that already support BSC."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["BNB Token Maker handles the contract for you. You provide the configuration, and your wallet deploys the result to BNB Smart Chain. Ownership of the deployed contract belongs to the wallet that deploys it. For a full step-by-step, see ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/create-bep20-token","children":"how to create a BEP-20 token"}],"; for terminology, the ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/bnb-token-generator","children":"BNB token generator"}]," page explains BNB vs BEP-20. Looking to launch a community token instead? See ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/create-meme-coin-bnb-chain","children":"how to create a meme coin on BNB Smart Chain"}],"."]}]]}]]}]}]
